{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Let us pass, pray, through your land.</b> You have no cause to raise a claim about the inheritance of the land of Israel. Just as you have not paid the debt, do us a small favor — let us pass through your land." "<b>And we will not drink water from a well.</b> He should have said 'water from cisterns.' Rather, thus said Moses: even though we have in our hand manna to eat and a well to drink from, we will not drink from it, but we will buy from you food and water for your benefit. From here: a guest, even though he has food to eat, should buy from the innkeeper, in order to benefit his host (Tanchuma)." "<b>The king's road we will go, etc.</b> We muzzle our animals, and they will not turn this way and that to eat (there)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:46.009841229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}